# debug/ — log bundles for sharing

`studiomind debug-bundle` copies the most recent session log from
`~/StudioMind/logs/` into this folder. The .gitignore is set up so
that:

- `debug/*.log` is committed (so `git push` shares the bundle)
- everything else in `debug/` (screenshots, scratch audio) is ignored

Old log bundles that were already pushed can be deleted at any time
once they're no longer needed:

  rm debug/session-*.log
  git add -u debug/
  git commit -m "Clean up old debug bundles"
